{"id": "tea:yogakundali-upanisad:1.19-39-summary", "source": "src:yogakundali-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "1.19-39 (summary)"}, "paraphrase": "Kumbhaka is twofold, sahita and kevala; sahita is of four kinds: sūrya(bheda), ujjāyī, śītalī and bhastrī. Methods and counts are not reproduced here.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["body-breath"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["practice"], "practices": ["prc:sahita-kumbhaka", "prc:kevala-kumbhaka"], "restricted": true, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "sourced", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": [{"phase": "C", "date": "2026-09-29", "method": "text-locate", "queries": ["e-text yogakundali-upanisad 1.19-39 (summary)"], "evidence": ["catalog:raw_etexts:108_Upanishads", "text:sources_raw/raw_etexts/vedaH/misc/upaniShat/mixedPF/108_Upanishads.md"], "result": "confirmed", "note": "E-text 1.19-39 (summary) located; the passage matches the paraphrase (it begins: 'prāṇarodhamathedānīṃ pravakṣyāmi samāsataḥ | prāṇaśca dehagovāyurāyāmaḥ kumbhakaḥ smṛtaḥ || 19 || sa eva…').", "by": "sourcing:U04-minor-upanisads"}]}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:yogakundali-upanisad:1.2", "source": "src:yogakundali-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "1.2"}, "paraphrase": "Of these, the breath is conquered by moderate diet, posture and the moving of the power (śakticālana).", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["body-breath"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["practice"], "practices": ["prc:mitahara", "prc:sakticalana"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "sourced", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": [{"phase": "C", "date": "2026-09-29", "method": "text-locate", "queries": ["e-text yogakundali-upanisad 1.2"], "evidence": ["catalog:raw_etexts:108_Upanishads", "text:sources_raw/raw_etexts/vedaH/misc/upaniShat/mixedPF/108_Upanishads.md"], "result": "confirmed", "note": "E-text 1.2 located in the e-text; the passage matches the paraphrase.", "by": "sourcing:U04-minor-upanisads"}]}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:yogakundali-upanisad:1.40-52", "source": "src:yogakundali-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "1.40-52"}, "paraphrase": "The three bandhas — mūla, uḍḍīyāna and jālandhara — are to be practised.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["body-breath"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["practice"], "practices": ["prc:bandha-traya"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "sourced", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": [{"phase": "C", "date": "2026-09-29", "method": "text-locate", "queries": ["e-text yogakundali-upanisad 1.40-52"], "evidence": ["catalog:raw_etexts:108_Upanishads", "text:sources_raw/raw_etexts/vedaH/misc/upaniShat/mixedPF/108_Upanishads.md"], "result": "confirmed", "note": "E-text 1.40-52 located; the passage matches the paraphrase (it begins: 'caturṇāmapi bhedānāṃ kumbhake samupasthite |bandhatrayamidaṃ kāryaṃ yogibhirvītakalmaṣaiḥ || 40 || prathamo…').", "by": "sourcing:U04-minor-upanisads"}]}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:yogakundali-upanisad:1.56-58", "source": "src:yogakundali-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "1.56-58"}, "paraphrase": "Disease arises from sleeping by day, keeping awake at night, excess of sex, crowds, suppressing the urges, unwholesome food and strain; the diseased practitioner then gives up yoga, thinking it caused the illness — this is the first obstacle.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["body-breath"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["practice"], "obstacles": ["obs:yogakundali-ten-vighnas"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "sourced", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": [{"phase": "C", "date": "2026-09-29", "method": "text-locate", "queries": ["e-text yogakundali-upanisad 1.56-58"], "evidence": ["catalog:raw_etexts:108_Upanishads", "text:sources_raw/raw_etexts/vedaH/misc/upaniShat/mixedPF/108_Upanishads.md"], "result": "confirmed", "note": "E-text 1.56-58 located; the passage matches the paraphrase (it begins: 'divā suptirniśāyāṃ tu jāgarādatimaithunāt | bahusaṅkramaṇaṃ nityaṃ rodhānmūtra-purīṣayoḥ || 56 ||…').", "by": "sourcing:U04-minor-upanisads"}]}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:yogakundali-upanisad:1.59-61", "source": "src:yogakundali-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "1.59-61"}, "paraphrase": "Ten obstacles: disease, doubt, heedlessness, sloth, sleep, withdrawal of interest, delusion, and further obstacles (readings uncertain) ending with failure to attain the truth of yoga; the wise should overcome them.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["body-breath"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["practice"], "obstacles": ["obs:yogakundali-ten-vighnas"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "sourced", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": [{"phase": "C", "date": "2026-09-29", "method": "text-locate", "queries": ["e-text yogakundali-upanisad 1.59-61"], "evidence": ["catalog:raw_etexts:108_Upanishads", "text:sources_raw/raw_etexts/vedaH/misc/upaniShat/mixedPF/108_Upanishads.md"], "result": "confirmed", "note": "This is on the skeleton's least-sure list. The e-text is located; it misnumbers v. 59 as '51'. The ten obstacles read: (1) roga, (2) saṃśaya, (3) pramattatā, (4) ālasya, (5) nidrā, (6) virati, (7) bhrānti, (8) viṣama, (9) 'anākhya' (unnamed), (10) alabdhi yogatattvasya. The readings of nos. 8 and 9 are indeed doubtful, as the entry says.", "by": "sourcing:U04-minor-upanisads"}]}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:yogakundali-upanisad:1.62-86", "source": "src:yogakundali-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "1.62-86"}, "paraphrase": "The kuṇḍalinī, roused like a serpent struck with a stick, enters the suṣumnā, pierces the knots of Brahmā, Viṣṇu and Rudra and the six lotuses, and unites with Śiva in the thousand-petalled lotus; then the world is seen to arise and dissolve falsely, like silver in mother-of-pearl.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "experiential", "naya": null, "path": ["body-breath", "meditation"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["body-layers", "powers-experiences", "karma-liberation"], "concepts": ["cpt:kundalini", "cpt:three-granthis", "cpt:cakras"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "sourced", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": [{"phase": "C", "date": "2026-09-29", "method": "text-locate", "queries": ["e-text yogakundali-upanisad 1.62-86"], "evidence": ["catalog:raw_etexts:108_Upanishads", "text:sources_raw/raw_etexts/vedaH/misc/upaniShat/mixedPF/108_Upanishads.md"], "result": "confirmed", "note": "E-text 1.62-86 located; the passage matches the paraphrase (it begins: 'prāṇābhyāsastataḥ kāryo nityaṃ sattva-sthayā dhiyā | suṣumnā līyate cittaṃ tathā vāyuḥ pradhāvati || 62 ||…').", "by": "sourcing:U04-minor-upanisads"}]}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:yogakundali-upanisad:1.7-18-summary", "source": "src:yogakundali-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "1.7-18 (summary)"}, "paraphrase": "Śakticālana — moving the kuṇḍalī from her place toward the brows — and sarasvatī-cālana are described; the text says they cure abdominal diseases. Recorded summary-only.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["body-breath"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["practice"], "practices": ["prc:sakticalana"], "restricted": true, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "sourced", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": [{"phase": "C", "date": "2026-09-29", "method": "text-locate", "queries": ["e-text yogakundali-upanisad 1.7-18 (summary)"], "evidence": ["catalog:raw_etexts:108_Upanishads", "text:sources_raw/raw_etexts/vedaH/misc/upaniShat/mixedPF/108_Upanishads.md"], "result": "confirmed", "note": "E-text 1.7-18 (summary) located; the passage matches the paraphrase (it begins: 'kuṇḍalyeva bhavecchaktistāṃ tu sañcālayedbudhaḥ |svasthānādābhruvormadhyaṃ śakticālanamucyate || 7 ||…').", "by": "sourcing:U04-minor-upanisads"}]}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:yogakundali-upanisad:2.1-13", "source": "src:yogakundali-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "2.1-13"}, "paraphrase": "The khecarī-vidyā is to be learnt from a guru who knows it from text, meaning and practice; its mantra (melana) comes only from the guru's mouth; it must be kept secret.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["general"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["teacher-transmission", "practice"], "practices": ["prc:khecari-mudra"], "concepts": ["cpt:secrecy-and-eligibility"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "sourced", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": [{"phase": "C", "date": "2026-09-29", "method": "text-locate", "queries": ["e-text yogakundali-upanisad 2.1-13"], "evidence": ["catalog:raw_etexts:108_Upanishads", "text:sources_raw/raw_etexts/vedaH/misc/upaniShat/mixedPF/108_Upanishads.md"], "result": "confirmed", "note": "E-text 2.1-13 located; the passage matches the paraphrase (it begins: 'athāhaṃ sampravakṣyāmi vidyāṃ khecarisañjñikām | yathā vijñānavānasyāloke'sminnajaro'maraḥ || 1 ||…').", "by": "sourcing:U04-minor-upanisads"}]}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:yogakundali-upanisad:2.28-49-summary", "source": "src:yogakundali-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "2.28-49 (summary)"}, "paraphrase": "Bodily procedures of khecarī are described; they are not reproduced here. The text warns that they must be done gradually, never all at once, or the body perishes, and gives a long period of practice.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["body-breath"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["practice"], "practices": ["prc:khecari-mudra"], "restricted": true, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "sourced", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": [{"phase": "C", "date": "2026-09-29", "method": "text-locate", "queries": ["e-text yogakundali-upanisad 2.28-49 (summary)"], "evidence": ["catalog:raw_etexts:108_Upanishads", "text:sources_raw/raw_etexts/vedaH/misc/upaniShat/mixedPF/108_Upanishads.md"], "result": "confirmed", "note": "E-text 2.28-49 (summary) located; the passage matches the paraphrase (it begins: 'tālumūlaṃ samutkṛṣya saptavāsaramātmavit |svagurūktaprakāreṇa malaṃ sarvaṃ viśodhayet || 28 ||…').", "by": "sourcing:U04-minor-upanisads"}]}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:yogakundali-upanisad:3.14-17", "source": "src:yogakundali-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "3.14-17"}, "paraphrase": "Fire hidden in wood appears only by churning; a lamp in a pot shows only when the pot breaks — the guru's word breaks it; the guru is the helmsman across saṃsāra.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["general"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["teacher-transmission"], "concepts": ["cpt:guru"], "cross_refs": ["tea:yogasikha-upanisad:6.76-79"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "sourced", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": [{"phase": "C", "date": "2026-09-29", "method": "text-locate", "queries": ["e-text yogakundali-upanisad 3.14-17"], "evidence": ["catalog:raw_etexts:108_Upanishads", "text:sources_raw/raw_etexts/vedaH/misc/upaniShat/mixedPF/108_Upanishads.md"], "result": "confirmed", "note": "E-text 3.14-17 located; the passage matches the paraphrase (it begins: 'samādhimekena samamamṛtaṃ yānti yoginaḥ | yathā'gnirdārumadhyastho nottiṣṭhenmathanaṃ vinā || 14 || vinā…').", "by": "sourcing:U04-minor-upanisads"}]}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:yogakundali-upanisad:3.18-19", "source": "src:yogakundali-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "3.18-19"}, "paraphrase": "Speech sprouts in parā, puts forth two leaves in paśyantī, buds in madhyamā and blossoms in vaikharī; by reversing this order sound is dissolved.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "experiential", "naya": null, "path": ["sound", "meditation"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["sound-language"], "concepts": ["cpt:levels-of-speech"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "sourced", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": [{"phase": "C", "date": "2026-09-29", "method": "text-locate", "queries": ["e-text yogakundali-upanisad 3.18-19"], "evidence": ["catalog:raw_etexts:108_Upanishads", "text:sources_raw/raw_etexts/vedaH/misc/upaniShat/mixedPF/108_Upanishads.md"], "result": "confirmed", "note": "E-text 3.18-19 located; the passage matches the paraphrase (it begins: 'abhyāsavāsanāśaktyā tarantibhavasāgaram | parāyāmaṅkurībhūya paśyantyāṃ dvidalīkṛtā || 18 ||…').", "by": "sourcing:U04-minor-upanisads"}]}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
